1. Take all my comfort of thy worth and truth.  
2. Serving with looks his sacred majesty;  
3. And yet methinks I have astronomy,  
4. Which I new pay as if not paid before.  
5. From sullen earth, sings hymns at heaven's gate;  
6. To find where your true image pictured lies;  
7. With what I most enjoy contented least;  
8. Cheered and cheque'd even by the self-same sky,  
